“A vampire’s greatest weakness isn’t sunlight or silver — it’s research.”
 — Regional Director T. Virelli, Starbucks Adventuring Division

Vampires are widely varied across the multiverse. However, for Delver’s Paradise, there is only one major species you need to worry about. The so-called Nocthollow vampires are fairly typical specimens. The function as follows:

Strengths: When not subject to one of their weaknesses, vampires are supernaturally strong and fast and nearly impossible to kill. They frequently have enchanted weapons and armor, and can bite you to suck your blood and heal themselves. If not thoroughly destroyed, they can revivify through blood, usually provided by their minions. Most Nocthollow vampires hold social positions of power, and thus have retainers and servants to protect them.

Magic: All known Nocthollow vampires are capable of learning a form of blood magic whose practitioners call themselves Warlocks. They can summon undead, fire eldretch fire from their hands, and various other potent magic effects. Not all vampires are good at this; mostly the nobility and other older and well-educated creatures. This magic is also well known for addicting the subjects (blood doners) to the touch of the practitioner. Don’t let them cut you.

Vulnerabilities: They burn quickly, both via direct fire and sunlight. They are driven from garlic, cannot enter a house uninvited. Many of their powers shut down while in contact with wood or silver, or when presented with the power of True Faith. They are also significantly weaker during the day, whether in direct sunlight or not.
